<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1">
<title>For Maalkin 💗</title>
<style>
body{
margin:0;min-height:100vh;display:flex;align-items:center;
justify-content:center;text-align:center;
font-family:Arial,sans-serif;
background:linear-gradient(135deg,#fff0f6,#ffd6e5);
color:#603344;padding:20px
}
.card{
max-width:500px;padding:35px 25px;border-radius:30px;
background:white;box-shadow:0 15px 50px #d99aaa55
}
h1{color:#d94d7b;font-size:42px}
.heart{font-size:55px}
button{
background:#e65383;color:white;border:0;
padding:16px 25px;border-radius:30px;
font-size:17px;font-weight:bold
}
#surprise{
display:none;margin-top:25px;padding:20px;
background:#fff5f8;border-radius:20px;
line-height:1.7;font-size:17px
}
</style>
</head>

<body>
<div class="card">

<div class="heart">🎀</div>

<p>A tiny birthday surprise for</p>

<h1>Maalkin 💗</h1>

<p>Happy Birthday to someone who is simply <b>everything.</b> 🫶🏻</p>

<button onclick="document.getElementById('surprise').style.display='block'">
💌 Open your little surprise
</button>

<div id="surprise">
🌷✨ <b>Your surprise</b> ✨🌷
<br><br>

I didn't need a big gift to tell you this. ❤️
<br><br>

I just wanted you to know that
<b>everything about you</b> is special to me —
your smile, your vibe, the way you talk,
and all those little things you probably
don't even notice. 💗
<br><br>

I hope your birthday gives you a hundred
reasons to smile.
<br><br>

<strong>Stay exactly the way you are, Maalkin. 💗</strong>
<br><br>

— Bunny 🐰
</div>

</div>
</body>
</html>
